---
layout: layouts/main.webc
---

<template webc:type="11ty" 11ty:type="njk">
{% html "meta" %}
<title>Privacy Policy | User Behavior in Design</title>
{% endhtml %}
</template>

<main class="container">
  <div class="card">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <h2>Who is behind this?</h2>
    <p>
      This site and the research are run by me — <a href="https://vukory.art/" target="_blank">Vukory</a>,
      a master&apos;s student at <a href="https://unze.ba/" target="_blank">University of Zenica</a>
      <span class="emojis" role="img" aria-label="Bosnia and Herzegovina">🇧🇦</span>.
    </p>
    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      This site uses Plausible for analytics. Plausible is a privacy-friendly,
      Open Source tool that uses no cookies. It&apos;s self-hosted by an SVGO
      maintainer, and <a href="https://plausible.falco.fun/survey.vukory.art" target="_blank">the dashboard</a>
      is fully public, so you can see exactly what I see. No secrets <span role="img" aria-label="uwu">:3</span>
    </p>
    <p>
      Plausible only picks up general information like which pages were visited,
      how long people stayed, and rough device info (device type, OS, country,
      browser). Nothing that points back to you. Also, if you use an ad blocker
      like uBlock Origin, it&apos;ll block Plausible by default.
    </p>
    <h2>Taking the survey?</h2>
    <p>
      When you submit your response, your answers travel securely (HTTPS) to a
      server I control. Along with your answers, the server also logs your IP
      address and browser details. I use this information to catch duplicate or
      spam submissions, and they get deleted together with any emails once the
      research wraps up.
    </p>
    <p>
      Your answers only ever appear in an aggregated form, fully anonymized in
      my thesis, never tied back to you.
    </p>
    <h2>Your email</h2>
    <p>
      Leaving your email is completely optional! It does exactly one job: allowing
      me to send you your single-use code for a free sticker pack. Once that code&apos;s
      been sent, your email has done its job and I will delete it, as there&apos;s no
      reason to hang onto it.
    </p>
    <h2>How long do I keep data?</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <span class="li-key">Emails and IP addresses</span> - deleted when the research ends
        (expected Q4 2027), or upon request
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="li-key">Your answers</span> - kept anonymized as part of the thesis
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Any questions? Feel free to reach out to me at <a href="mailto:hi@vukory.art" target="_blank">hi@vukory.art</a>! <span class="emojis" aria-hidden="true">💌</span>
    </p>
    <h2>Who helps to run this?</h2>
    <p>
      A few services keep all of this working behind the scenes:
    </p>
    <div class="table-container">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Third Party</th>
            <th>What they do</th>
            <th>Where</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><a href="https://github.com/" target="_blank">GitHub</a></td>
            <td>Delivers this website to your browser with GitHub Pages</td>
            <td>United States <span class="emojis" aria-hidden="true">🇺🇸</span></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Falco&apos;s Tea Party</td>
            <td>Self-Hosts <a href="https://plausible.falco.fun/survey.vukory.art" target="_blank">Plausible</a></td>
            <td>United Kingdom <span class="emojis" aria-hidden="true">🇬🇧</span></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><a href="https://contabo.com/" target="_blank">Contabo</a></td>
            <td>Hosts the server that stores survey responses</td>
            <td>United Kingdom <span class="emojis" aria-hidden="true">🇬🇧</span></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><a href="https://mailbox.org/" target="_blank">mailbox</a></td>
            <td>Hosts my inbox (your sticker code will get delivered from here)</td>
            <td>Germany <span class="emojis" aria-hidden="true">🇩🇪</span></td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
  <vuko-button id="return" href="/" @as="a">
    <span aria-hidden="true">←</span> <span>Return to Survey</span>
  </vuko-button>
</main>

<style>
  .container {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    width: calc(100% - var(--vuko-content-margin) * 2);
    margin: var(--vuko-content-margin) 0;
    max-width: var(--vuko-content-width);
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .card {
    position: relative;
  }

  .card::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset: -8px;
    background-image:
      url("/assets/flower-2.svg"),
      url("/assets/flower-1.svg");
    background-repeat: no-repeat;
    background-size: 6rem, 4rem;
    background-position:
      top right,
      bottom left;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  span.li-key {
    font-weight: bold;
  }

  .table-container {
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  table {
    text-align: left;
    border-spacing: 0;
    min-width: 100%;
  }

  th, td {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--vuko-subtext-color);
    padding: 0.4rem;
  }

  .emojis {
    font-family: var(--vuko-emoji);
  }

  #return {
    align-self: flex-start;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: .5rem;
  }
</style>
